    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "2. This is an appeal against acquittal recorded by learned Additional Sessions Judge/FTSC,\nHaridwar in Sessions Trial No. 228 of 2017.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 401,
      "end": 536,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Additional Sessions Judge/FTSC,\nHaridwar",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 461,
          "end": 501
        },
        {
          "text": "Sessions Trial No. 228 of 2017",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 505,
          "end": 535
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "By the impugned judgment, respondent was acquitted of the charge punishable under Section 376 IPC.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RLC",
      "start": 537,
      "end": 635,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 376",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 619,
          "end": 630
        },
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 631,
          "end": 634
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.38672471046447754
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "3. An application seeking leave to appeal has been filed by husband of the victim.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 636,
      "end": 719,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3249172568321228
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "As per office report, there is delay of 378 days in filing such application.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 720,
      "end": 796,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2606678903102875
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "4. It is contended on behalf of the appellant that since victim is deaf and dumb, therefore, this appeal is filed by her husband.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 797,
      "end": 927,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.21361789107322693
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "5. Proviso to Section 372 CrPC confers an independent right of appeal to the victim and the expression \"victim\" is defined under Section 2(wa) of CrPC, which is reproduced below:-",
      "rhetorical_role": "STA",
      "start": 928,
      "end": 1108,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 372",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 943,
          "end": 954
        },
        {
          "text": "CrPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 955,
          "end": 959
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 2(wa)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1058,
          "end": 1071
        },
        {
          "text": "CrPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1075,
          "end": 1079
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.15624025464057922
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "\"2(wa) \"victim\" means a person who has suffered any loss or injury caused by reason of the act or omission for which the accused person has been charged and the expression \"victim\" includes his or her guardian or legal heir.\"\n6.",
      "rhetorical_role": "STA",
      "start": 1109,
      "end": 1338,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1643528789281845
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Thus, this appeal against acquittal filed by husband of the victim would not be maintainable that too after delay of 378 days, when the victim can file appeal under proviso to Section 372 CrPC.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 1339,
      "end": 1532,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 372",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1515,
          "end": 1526
        },
        {
          "text": "CrPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1527,
          "end": 1531
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5316164493560791
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "7. In view of provision contained in Section 378(5) CrPC, delay in filing the application seeking leave to appeal cannot be condoned.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1534,
      "end": 1667,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 378(5)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1571,
          "end": 1585
        },
        {
          "text": "CrPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1586,
          "end": 1590
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.4348011016845703
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "CRLA/355/2023 on 19 September, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71254723/\n1 8.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1668,
      "end": 1763,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "CRLA/355/2023",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1669,
